---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { BOOTNODES, isTestnetLive, TESTNET_RPC_URL } from '../config/testnet';

const exampleBootnodes =
  isTestnetLive && BOOTNODES.length > 0
    ? BOOTNODES.join(',')
    : '/ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001';
---

<Layout
  title="Bootnodes"
  description="What bootnodes are and how to use them to join the Boing Network testnet."
>
  <article class="page-wrap-full">
    <header class="page-hero-full">
      <div class="page-wrap-inner">
        <span class="stage-badge-global">Testnet</span>
        <h1 class="page-title"><Icon name="network" size={32} class="title-icon" /> Bootnodes</h1>
        <p class="lead">
          Bootnodes are well-known peer addresses that your node <strong>dials on startup</strong> to join the testnet. Without them, your node would only discover peers on the same LAN (via mDNS).
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>
    <div class="page-wrap-inner bootnodes-content">
    <section class="section">
      <h2>What they are</h2>
      <p>When you run a node with P2P enabled (<code>--p2p-listen</code>), it needs to find other peers. On a local network, <strong>mDNS</strong> can discover nearby nodes. To join the <strong>public testnet</strong> from anywhere, your node must connect to at least one stable peer — a <strong>bootnode</strong>.</p>
      <p>Bootnodes are simply nodes that have a stable, publicly reachable address (IP + port). The team or community runs them and publishes their multiaddrs so new nodes can dial in and then discover more peers via gossip.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Format</h2>
      <p>A bootnode address is a <strong>multiaddr</strong>, for example:</p>
      <pre class="code-block"><code>{BOOTNODES[0] || '/ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001'}</code></pre>
      <p>You pass one or more bootnodes to your node with <code>--bootnodes</code> (comma-separated).</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>How to use</h2>
      {isTestnetLive ? (
        <>
          <p>Public testnet RPC is at <code>{TESTNET_RPC_URL}</code>. Use the official bootnode list below (also on <a href="/testnet/join">Join Testnet</a>):</p>
          <pre class="code-block"><code>{`./boing-node --p2p-listen /ip4/0.0.0.0/tcp/4001 \\
  --bootnodes ${exampleBootnodes} \\
  --validator --rpc-port 8545 --faucet-enable`}</code></pre>
          <p>For local dev only, run a <strong>local</strong> multi-node setup: start one node with <code>--p2p-listen /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001</code>, then start a second node with <code>--bootnodes /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001</code>.</p>
        </>
      ) : (
        <>
          <p>When public bootnodes are published, they will appear in this section and on <a href="/testnet/join">Join Testnet</a>. For local dev:</p>
          <pre class="code-block"><code>{`./boing-node --p2p-listen /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001 \\
  --bootnodes /ip4/127.0.0.1/tcp/4001 \\
  --validator --rpc-port 8545`}</code></pre>
        </>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Official testnet bootnodes</h2>
      {isTestnetLive && BOOTNODES.length > 0 ? (
        <>
          <p>Use these multiaddrs with <code>--bootnodes</code> (comma-separated). Also in <a href="/pdfs/TESTNET.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TESTNET (PDF)</a> and <a href="https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/blob/main/docs/TESTNET.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener">docs/TESTNET.md</a>.</p>
          <p class="muted small-print">Hosted Fly.io pair: validator then full node. Public JSON-RPC stays at <code>https://testnet-rpc.boing.network/</code>.</p>
          <pre class="code-block"><code>{BOOTNODES.join('\n')}</code></pre>
        </>
      ) : (
        <p>Bootnode multiaddrs will be published here when the public testnet endpoints are configured.</p>
      )}
    </section>

    <nav class="section nav-links">
      <a href="/testnet/join">← Join Testnet</a>
      <a href="/faucet">Faucet →</a>
    </nav>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .bootnodes-content { padding-bottom: 3rem; }
  .page-title { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; color: var(--text-primary); }
  .title-icon { color: var(--accent-teal); flex-shrink: 0; }
  .bootnodes-content h1 { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .lead { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .section { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .section h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; color: var(--text-primary); margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .section p { color: var(--text-secondary); }
  .section code { background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); padding: 0.15rem 0.4rem; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .code-block { background: rgba(0,0,0,0.3); border: 1px solid rgba(34,211,238,0.2); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1rem; overflow-x: auto; }
  .code-block code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .muted { color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .nav-links { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1rem; }
  .nav-links a { color: var(--accent-teal); font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .bootnodes-content { padding-bottom: 2rem; }
    .section { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .code-block { font-size: 0.85rem; padding: 0.75rem; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 375px) {
    .section { margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  }
</style>
